{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba WORDING-V2.md; nl -ba scorer-checks.log; nl -ba probe-v2-dry.log | sed -n '1,25p;63,70p'; nl -ba probe-v2-mutant.log\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# A sharpened link question, version 2 (D703; for council review before its cents probe)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose to probe a sharpened wording before the paid run (D703): keep Data Center reads total revenue and the 38 negatives, remove\n     4\tunsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part. The probe is harness-only: `window_test.py\n     5\tprobe-v2` replaces the READS and SIGN criteria texts in memory for its pass; no product file changes until a version is chosen.\n     6\t\n     7\t## 1. Prompt audit (the census's failure classes against the request sentences; AGENTS §6)\n     8\t\n     9\t| Failure class (census, `CENSUS-RESULT.md`) | The request sentence that produced it | The standard or decision on the case | Verdict |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| Part against whole, direction unsettled: v9–v14 at margins 0.03–0.09; v21–v9 flips between draws; whole-to-part and part-to-whole both occur | READS `candidate_reads_thesis`: \"a part read against its whole (...), or a quantity read against another it depends on (...)\": the second clause lets a whole \"depend on\" its part; no sentence says which reads when both fit | D537: the total carried the year's consensus and guidance that the segment's requests lacked; D260: a judgement is made against what the market expects (consensus, guidance, the stated plan) | **abstract** (two clauses, both directions, no tie-break) |\n    12\t| Across periods with an unsupported sign: v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together, 3 of 3; v35 (FY2028 total) reads v9 (FY2027 Data Center), 1 of 3 | no READS sentence on periods (`neither` covers only \"the same quantity for the same period and scope\"); every SIGN example is within one period | the arithmetic of a growth rate (a higher base lowers next year's growth at a given level); the dependency design §2: another period of the same quantity \"may be linked\" | **missing** |\n    13\t\n    14\t## 2. The wording (changes marked; every example from another industry, none names the covered company)\n    15\t\n    16\tREADS, `candidate_reads_thesis`, appended sentence:\n    17\t> When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no guidance,\n    18\t> consensus or reported figure for the quantity and full period the question asks about) is the one judged with the other's conclusion\n    19\t> in view.\n    20\t\n    21\tREADS, `neither`, appended clause (before \"sharing a company ...\"):\n    22\t> or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a retailer's\n    23\t> sales this year and its sales growth next year, when the text only names both)\n    24\t\n    25\tSIGN, `opposite`, added example:\n    26\t> ...; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth\n    27\t\n    28\t`thesis_reads_candidate` (\"for the same reasons with the roles swapped\") and the instructions are unchanged, so the tie-break applies\n    29\tboth ways: a part with guidance and a whole without would have the whole read the part. No direction is banned.\n    30\t\n    31\tSources (round 18 made the distinction explicit): the general tie-break and the periods clause are proposals this probe is authorized\n    32\tto test by D703, not rules already decided; D537 decided only the concrete case (Data Center revenue reading total revenue, the total\n    33\tcarrying the year's consensus), and D260 explains why guidance and consensus anchor a judgement (it governs judging, not linking). The\n    34\tbase-effect example is the arithmetic of a growth rate with the next-year level held fixed. The periods clause narrows the dependency\n    35\tdesign §2 (\"another period of the same quantity may be linked\") to \"when the supplied text states how\": a link across periods still\n    36\texists when the text gives the bridge (v35 reads v14: the FY2028 outlook translates growth into a level through the FY2027 base).\n    37\tRound 18 read the seq-148 request (dry archive, call 8744): the total carries Bloomberg's $393B FY2027 estimate, Data Center a Q1\n    38\tfigure of $75.25B (92% of the quarter): a full-year anchor against a partial-year one, so the tie-break gives v9 reads v14. Growth: 595\n    39\tcharacters across the three criteria texts (READS `candidate_reads_thesis` +269, `neither` +209, SIGN `opposite` +117; the READS\n    40\tcriteria repeat in every pair of a job, about 120 tokens a pair); written reason: the audit shows a missing case and an abstract clause, and nothing in the current texts\n    41\tduplicates them to cut.\n    42\t\n    43\t## 3. What the probe decides (registered before its answers: `expected-links-v2.json`)\n    44\t\n    45\tThe census's registration (R 1, W 38, O 66) with, for version 2 only (`expected-links-v2.json`): **W** for any link across periods\n    46\twhose shown text gives no bridge, the two unsupported links council R named (321:v16, v17 FY2028 growth against v16 FY2027 CPU; 1238:v9,\n    47\tv35 FY2028 total against v9 FY2027 Data Center; round 18 showed the gate passing without this); **F**, the base-effect sign, a growth\n    48\trate reading an earlier period's revenue amount with the sign together (321:v8, 321:v9, 321:v14). Version 2: R 1, W 40, O 61, F 3;\n    49\t1238:v14 stays O and is reported. Gate: the known positive right in 3 of 3 draws, no W link, no F link. $0 checks on the stored census\n    50\tanswers (`scorer-checks.log`): as stored, FAIL on 321:v16 and 1238:v9; with 321:v16 made \"neither\" and 1238:v9 kept, FAIL; with both\n    51\tmade \"neither\", PASS; 321:v16 linked with the sign opposite, FAIL; 321:v14 linked together, FAIL. Reported beside: every O pair\n    52\tagainst the census, and the margins.\n    53\t- **Pass:** version 2 becomes the candidate for the paid design (a product version built and reviewed first).\n    54\t- **Fail on the known positive or a W link:** the current wording stays the candidate with its measured risks (D702).\n    55\t- **Fail on F only:** the base-effect sentence did not take; reported, the current wording's risk stands.\n    56\t- **A ceiling stop before draw 3 completes:** an incomplete probe, no verdict (round 18: the observed job shapes price at about $0.034\n    57\t  for three draws; the all-SIGN stress shape at 0.37 tokens a byte at about $0.074 against $0.0734 left).\n    58\t\n    59\t## 4. The probe\n    60\t\n    61\t`window_test.py probe-v2 <scratch> <draw> <ledger> 0.10`: the census pass with the version-2 texts patched into `links.READS` and\n    62\t`links.SIGN` for the pass; every link job is new (the July answers do not match the new texts), so the seq-148 jobs are bought. Three\n    63\tdraws on D700's ledger (spent $0.0266, $0.0734 left); priced as the census (a draw settles about $0.009 at the ledger's rule; the READS\n    64\trequests grow by about 120 tokens a pair). The completeness check, equality with old-2 and the paid-transport record apply as in the\n    65\tcensus; `draw.json` records the wording.\n     1\tregistration: 1 R, 38 W, 66 O\n     2\tno draws: refused: three census draws are required, got 0\n     3\tthree folders without draw.json: refused: 0054109/scratchpad/window/census-dry: no draw.json (not a census draw)\n     4\tthe dry draw x3: refused: /scratchpad/window/census-reuse-dry: not a paid draw (transport 'dry')\n     5\tfake \"reads\" answers everywhere: wrong 114 known positive right 3 gate False\n     6\ta missing READS answer: refused: dry: no READS answer for the registered pair 1262:v1\n     7\tcontrol (only the known positive, together): gate True right 3\n     8\tmutant (known positive with sign opposite): gate False\n     9\tmutant (known positive reversed): gate False\n    10\tcensus draws under --v2: s-2026-11-21/census-1: wording None, expected 'v2'\n    11\tcensus answers scored on the v2 registration (positive control for F): wrong [('c1', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'together'), ('c2', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'together'), ('c3', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'together')] gate False\n    12\t-- version-2 registration checks (round 18) --\n    13\tcensus answers as stored: gate False wrong ['1238:v9', '321:v16']\n    14\t321:v16 made \"neither\", 1238:v9 kept (round 18 counterexample): gate False wrong [('c2', '1238:v9', 'v35 reads v9', 'together')]\n    15\tboth no-bridge pairs made \"neither\": gate True O links kept ['v1', 'v14', 'v16', 'v9', 'v14']\n    16\t321:v16 linked with the sign opposite: gate False wrong [('c1', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'opposite')]\n    17\t321:v14 linked together (F): gate False wrong [('c1', '321:v14', 'v17 reads v14', 'together')]\n     1\ttotals: {'items': 2077, 'extracted': 1884, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 193, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0, 'evidence': 5120, 'new_views': 43, 'judged': 1616, 'changed': 882, 'closed': 1} seconds: 380\n     2\tlast completed seq 1884 old-2 1884\n     3\tviews: rebuilt 43 stored 43 equal\n     4\tview_keys: rebuilt 43 stored 43 equal\n     5\tevidence: rebuilt 5102 stored 5102 equal\n     6\tevidence_links: rebuilt 6306 stored 6306 equal\n     7\tjudgements: rebuilt 1616 stored 1616 equal\n     8\trungs: rebuilt 137 stored 137 equal\n     9\tview_switches: rebuilt 44 stored 44 equal\n    10\tsuccessions: rebuilt 2 stored 2 equal\n    11\tdependencies: rebuilt 0 stored 0 equal\n    12\t{\n    13\t \"equal to old-2\": true,\n    14\t \"link jobs asked\": 28,\n    15\t \"questions in them\": 210,\n    16\t \"old-2's refused answers met again\": [\n    17\t  \"cfd45dde68ce\",\n    18\t  \"907eb29065b7\",\n    19\t  \"6d0c31a8460d\",\n    20\t  \"137e5f747345\"\n    21\t ],\n    22\t \"left unmet\": [],\n    23\t \"link rows written\": 0\n    24\t}\n    25\t8 eligible ['v1'] not eligible 3\n    63\t1828 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    64\t1874 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    65\tledger: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False} complete: True [] jobs carrying version 2: 28\n    66\tproposals: 105\n    67\texit 0\n     1\tmutant (texts not patched) caught: RuntimeError ins resumable: linking: link question failed: Stop: a link job does not carry the version-2 criteria: not sent | inner calls: 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba window_test.py | sed -n '303,391p'; nl -ba expected_links.py | sed -n '21,29p;70,102p'; rg -n '321:v(8|9|14|16)|1238:v(9|14)|148:v9' expected-links-v2.json; nl -ba read_census.py | sed -n '69,157p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba window_test.py | sed -n '303,391p'; nl -ba expected_links.py | sed -n '21,29p;70,102p'; rg -n '321:v(8|9|14|16)|1238:v(9|14)|148:v9' expected-links-v2.json; nl -ba read_census.py | sed -n '69,157p'\"","aggregated_output":"   303\t# ---------- version 2 of the link question (WORDING-V2.md, D703): a harness-only probe ----------\n   304\t\n   305\tV2_TIE_BREAK = (\" When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no \"\n   306\t                \"guidance, consensus or reported figure for the quantity and full period the question asks about) is the one judged \"\n   307\t                \"with the other's conclusion in view.\")\n   308\tV2_PERIODS = (\" or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a \"\n   309\t              \"retailer's sales this year and its sales growth next year, when the text only names both);\")\n   310\tV2_BASE = \"; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth)\"\n   311\t\n   312\t\n   313\tdef wording_v2():\n   314\t    \"\"\"The version-2 READS and SIGN criteria: the current texts with the three changes of WORDING-V2.md §2 (each anchored on a unique\n   315\t    phrase of the current text, so a moved text fails loudly).\"\"\"\n   316\t    reads, sign = dict(links.READS), dict(links.SIGN)\n   317\t    reads[links.CANDIDATE_READS] = reads[links.CANDIDATE_READS] + V2_TIE_BREAK\n   318\t    anchor = \"for the same period and scope;\"\n   319\t    assert reads[links.NEITHER].count(anchor) == 1\n   320\t    reads[links.NEITHER] = reads[links.NEITHER].replace(anchor, \"for the same period and scope,\" + V2_PERIODS)\n   321\t    tail = \"a retailer's markdowns and its gross margin)\"\n   322\t    assert sign[links.OPPOSITE].endswith(tail)\n   323\t    sign[links.OPPOSITE] = sign[links.OPPOSITE][:-1] + V2_BASE\n   324\t    return reads, sign\n   325\t\n   326\t\n   327\tdef with_wording_v2(run):\n   328\t    reads, sign = wording_v2()\n   329\t    original = links.READS, links.SIGN\n   330\t    links.READS, links.SIGN = reads, sign\n   331\t    try:\n   332\t        return run()\n   333\t    finally:\n   334\t        links.READS, links.SIGN = original\n   335\t\n   336\t\n   337\tdef probe_pass(folder, draw, inner, ledger_state, transport_kind):\n   338\t    \"\"\"One version-2 draw into `folder`: every link job asked with the version-2 texts (none matches a July request, so all are sent to\n   339\t    `inner`), the writer handed no link. Every request must carry the version-2 texts (checked as it is sent). Writes `draw.json`; the\n   340\t    draw is counted only when it is complete, ended equal to old-2 with no link row, and the ledger neither stopped nor overran.\"\"\"\n   341\t    reads, sign = wording_v2()\n   342\t    carried = []\n   343\t\n   344\t    def link_answer(request):\n   345\t        texts = [q['criteria'] for q in request['questions'].values()]\n   346\t        expected = reads if next(iter(request['questions'])).startswith('reads__') else sign\n   347\t        if any(criteria != {k: v for k, v in expected.items() if k in criteria} for criteria in texts):\n   348\t            raise july_test.Stop('a link job does not carry the version-2 criteria: not sent')\n   349\t        carried.append(len(texts))\n   350\t        return inner(request)\n   351\t    result = with_wording_v2(lambda: without_links(lambda: replay_window(folder, link_answer)))\n   352\t    state = ledger_state()\n   353\t    whole, problems = complete(result)\n   354\t    counted = result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0 and whole and bool(carried) and not state.get('stopped') and not state.get('overrun')\n   355\t    (folder / 'draw.json').write_text(json.dumps({'draw': draw, 'wording': 'v2', 'transport': transport_kind, 'counted': counted,\n   356\t                                                  'complete': whole, 'problems': problems, 'equal to old-2': result['equal to old-2'],\n   357\t                                                  'jobs carrying version 2': len(carried), 'ledger': state}, indent=1))\n   358\t    print('ledger:', state, 'complete:', whole, problems, 'jobs carrying version 2:', len(carried))\n   359\t    return counted\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\tdef probe_v2_dry(scratch):\n   363\t    \"\"\"$0: the version-2 pass with every pair answered \"reads\", sign together: complete, equal to old-2, every job carrying the\n   364\t    version-2 texts, 105 proposals.\"\"\"\n   365\t    counted = probe_pass(scratch / 'probe-v2-dry', 'dry', july_test.fake_jev(Everything()), lambda: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False}, 'dry')\n   366\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{scratch / \"probe-v2-dry\" / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   367\t    proposed = sum(len(json.loads(r)['proposed']) for (r,) in conn.execute(\"select record_json from link_selections where status='proposed'\"))\n   368\t    print('proposals:', proposed)\n   369\t    return counted and proposed == 105\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\tdef probe_v2(scratch, draw, ledger_path, approved):\n   373\t    \"\"\"One paid version-2 draw on D700's ledger (the same checks as `census`: approved finite ceiling equal to the ledger's, launcher\n   374\t    registered, stop gate installed).\"\"\"\n   375\t    budget = july_test.budget_module()\n   376\t    if not (isinstance(approved, float) and math.isfinite(approved) and 0 < approved <= CENSUS_CEILING):\n   377\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling must be a finite amount above 0 and at most ${CENSUS_CEILING}')\n   378\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   379\t    ceiling = ledger.read()['ceiling']\n   380\t    if not (isinstance(ceiling, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(ceiling) and ceiling == approved):\n   381\t        raise SystemExit(f'the ledger ceiling {ceiling!r} is not the approved ${approved}: refused')\n   382\t    if draw not in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   383\t        raise SystemExit('draw must be 1, 2 or 3')\n   384\t    label = f'probe-v2-{draw}'\n   385\t    lock_handle = open(Path(ledger_path).with_name(f'{label}.launcher.lock'), 'a+')\n   386\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher(label, lock_handle):\n   387\t        raise SystemExit(f'another launch of {label} is running')\n   388\t    budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   389\t    try:\n   390\t        return probe_pass(scratch / label, draw, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger.read, 'paid')\n   391\t    finally:\n    21\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    22\tREQUIRED = {('v9', 'v14'): 'Data Center revenue read against total revenue: D537\\'s clear case, the known positive'}\n    23\tFINANCING = {'v1', 'v2', 'v15', 'v29', 'v32', 'v36'}\n    24\tBASE_EFFECT_READ = {'v8', 'v9', 'v14', 'v16'}      # FY2027 revenue amounts; v17 is FY2028 total revenue growth\n    25\tNO_BRIDGE = ('321:v16', '1238:v9')                # FY2027 CPU against FY2028 growth; FY2027 Data Center against FY2028 total (round 18)\n    26\tREVENUE = {'v8', 'v9', 'v14', 'v16', 'v17', 'v21', 'v35'}\n    27\tMARGIN = {'v28', 'v33'}\n    28\tCREDIT = {'v1', 'v2'}\n    29\tOPEN_FINANCING = {frozenset({'v1', 'v2'}): 'AI-cloud credit support sits inside all customer and cloud-provider credit support; either may read the other',\n    70\t    print('|---|---|---|---|---|---|')\n    71\t    for seq, thesis in rows:\n    72\t        kind, direction, reason = classify(new_at[seq], thesis)\n    73\t        counts[kind] += 1\n    74\t        out[f'{seq}:{thesis}'] = {'new': new_at[seq], 'shown': thesis, 'class': kind, 'direction': direction}\n    75\t        print(f'| {seq} | {new_at[seq]} | {thesis} | {kind} | {direction or \"\"} | {reason} |')\n    76\t    print(f'\\nPairs: {len(rows)}; R {counts[\"R\"]}, W {counts[\"W\"]}, O {counts[\"O\"]}. The seq-148 pairs were seen before this registration.')\n    77\t    (HERE / 'expected-links.json').write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1))\n    78\t    # version 2's registration (WORDING-V2.md §3, written before its probe's answers): the census's classes plus F, the base-effect\n    79\t    # sign council R round 17 named: a growth rate reading an earlier period's revenue amount with the sign together\n    80\t    v2 = json.loads(json.dumps(out))\n    81\t    for key, entry in v2.items():\n    82\t        if entry['new'] == 'v17' and entry['shown'] in BASE_EFFECT_READ:\n    83\t            entry.update({'class': 'F', 'direction': None, 'forbidden': ('v17 reads ' + entry['shown'], 'together')})\n    84\t    for key in NO_BRIDGE:            # round 18: the shown text gives no bridge across the periods, so any accepted link fails\n    85\t        v2[key].update({'class': 'W', 'direction': None, 'forbidden': None})\n    86\t    (HERE / 'expected-links-v2.json').write_text(json.dumps(v2, indent=1))\n    87\t    print(f\"\\nVersion 2 adds F (forbidden: v17 reads an FY2027 revenue amount with the sign together): {sorted(k for k, e in v2.items() if e['class'] == 'F')}; \"\n    88\t          f\"and W for any link across periods with no bridge in the shown text: {list(NO_BRIDGE)}; 1238:v14 stays O and is reported.\")\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    92\t    main()\n38: \"148:v9\": {\n128: \"321:v14\": {\n138: \"321:v16\": {\n145: \"321:v9\": {\n161: \"321:v8\": {\n489: \"1238:v14\": {\n507: \"1238:v9\": {\n    69\tdef score(draws, expected):\n    70\t    \"\"\"draws: [(name, decisions)]. Returns (rows, summary); refuses when a registered pair has no READS answer in a draw.\"\"\"\n    71\t    rows, wrong, missed, right, fragile, positive = [], [], [], [], [], []\n    72\t    for key, reg in expected.items():\n    73\t        seq, thesis = int(key.split(':')[0]), key.split(':')[1]\n    74\t        cells = []\n    75\t        for name, answers in draws:\n    76\t            entry = answers.get((seq, thesis))\n    77\t            if entry is None or entry['p'] is None:\n    78\t                raise Refused(f'{name}: no READS answer for the registered pair {key}')\n    79\t            direction, sign = linked(entry, reg['new'], thesis)\n    80\t            m = margin(entry)\n    81\t            short = {'candidate_reads_thesis': 'new→', 'thesis_reads_candidate': '←new', 'neither': 'none'}[entry['reads']]\n    82\t            cell = f\"{short} {entry['p'][entry['reads']]:.2f} (m {m:.2f})\" + (f\"; {entry['sign']} {entry['sp'][entry['sign']]:.2f}\" if entry['sign'] else '')\n    83\t            if reg['class'] == 'R':\n    84\t                if direction is None:\n    85\t                    verdict = 'missed'\n    86\t                elif direction == reg['direction'] and sign == REQUIRED_SIGN:\n    87\t                    verdict = 'right'\n    88\t                else:\n    89\t                    verdict = 'WRONG'\n    90\t                positive.append(verdict == 'right')\n    91\t            elif reg['class'] == 'W':\n    92\t                verdict = 'WRONG' if direction else 'right'\n    93\t            elif reg['class'] == 'F':\n    94\t                verdict = 'WRONG' if (direction, sign) == tuple(reg['forbidden']) else (f'linked: {direction} ({sign})' if direction else 'no link')\n    95\t            else:\n    96\t                verdict = f'linked: {direction} ({sign})' if direction else 'no link'\n    97\t            if verdict == 'WRONG':\n    98\t                wrong.append((name, key, direction, sign))\n    99\t            elif verdict == 'missed':\n   100\t                missed.append((name, key))\n   101\t            elif verdict == 'right' and reg['class'] == 'R':\n   102\t                right.append((name, key))\n   103\t            if (direction or reg['class'] == 'R') and m < 0.10:\n   104\t                fragile.append((name, key, m))\n   105\t            cells.append(f'{cell} → {verdict}')\n   106\t        rows.append((seq, reg, thesis, cells))\n   107\t    gate = not wrong and bool(positive) and all(positive)\n   108\t    return rows, {'right': right, 'missed': missed, 'wrong': wrong, 'fragile': fragile, 'gate': gate}\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef counted_draws(folders, wording=None):\n   112\t    if len(folders) != 3:\n   113\t        raise Refused(f'three census draws are required, got {len(folders)}')\n   114\t    seen = []\n   115\t    for folder in folders:\n   116\t        record_path = Path(folder) / 'draw.json'\n   117\t        if not record_path.exists():\n   118\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: no draw.json (not a census draw)')\n   119\t        record = json.loads(record_path.read_text())\n   120\t        if record.get('transport') != 'paid':\n   121\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: not a paid draw (transport {record.get(\"transport\")!r})')\n   122\t        if record.get('wording') != wording:\n   123\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: wording {record.get(\"wording\")!r}, expected {wording!r}')\n   124\t        if not record.get('counted'):\n   125\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: the draw was not counted: {record.get(\"problems\")}')\n   126\t        seen.append(record['draw'])\n   127\t    if sorted(seen) != ['1', '2', '3']:\n   128\t        raise Refused(f'the draws must be 1, 2 and 3, got {seen}')\n   129\t    return [(Path(f).name, decisions(Path(f) / 'views.sqlite')) for f in folders]\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\tdef main(folders):\n   133\t    wording = None\n   134\t    if folders and folders[0] == '--v2':\n   135\t        wording, folders = 'v2', folders[1:]\n   136\t    expected = json.loads((HERE / ('expected-links-v2.json' if wording == 'v2' else 'expected-links.json')).read_text())\n   137\t    draws = counted_draws(folders, wording)\n   138\t    rows, summary = score(draws, expected)\n   139\t    print('# Census of the link decisions over the window, scored against the registered reading\\n')\n   140\t    print('| seq | new | shown | class | registered | ' + ' | '.join(name for name, _ in draws) + ' |')\n   141\t    print('|---|---|---|---|---|' + '---|' * len(draws))\n   142\t    for seq, reg, thesis, cells in rows:\n   143\t        print(f\"| {seq} | {reg['new']} | {thesis} | {reg['class']} | {reg['direction'] or ''} | \" + ' | '.join(cells) + ' |')\n   144\t    print('\\nDraws: 3 (' + ('version 2: every link job asked fresh, the seq-148 jobs included).' if wording == 'v2' else\n   145\t                             'the seq-148 jobs of each answered by its paired July sample).'))\n   146\t    print(f\"Known positive right: {len(summary['right'])}; missed: {len(summary['missed'])} {summary['missed']}\")\n   147\t    print(f\"Wrong links: {len(summary['wrong'])} {summary['wrong']}\")\n   148\t    print(f\"Fragile (margin below 0.10 on a linked or required pair): {len(summary['fragile'])} {summary['fragile']}\")\n   149\t    print(f\"\\nGate (no wrong link in any draw; the known positive right in every draw): {'PASS' if summary['gate'] else 'FAIL'}\")\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   153\t    main(sys.argv[1:])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba codex-r18.md | tail -35; nl -ba ../../../poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10515,10523p;10556,10566p'; find /private/tmp/claude-501 -path '*probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite' -print\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba codex-r18.md | tail -35; nl -ba ../../../poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10515,10523p;10556,10566p'; find /private/tmp/claude-501 -path '*probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite' -print\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t**NOT READY.** The wording points toward the right July link, but the gate can pass while retaining one of the unsupported cross-period links this probe is meant to remove. I reproduced that false pass using the stored census answers. [Probe objective](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:36) · [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:83)\n     2\t\n     3\t### 1. Prompt audit\n     4\t\n     5\t- **Tie-break.** D537 supports letting the question with the weaker anchor read the better-anchored question when the relationship works both ways. D260 explains why consensus, guidance and reported figures matter. The general tie-break is a proposal authorized for this probe by D703. D537 decided the concrete Data Center case, and D260 governs judging. The audit should make that distinction explicit. [D537](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6457) · [D260](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3053) · [D703](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10556)\n     6\t- **Periods clause.** The older design permits links across periods. Requiring a mechanism in the supplied text is the proposed narrowing under D703. The generic retailer example is industry-neutral, but it needs to say that the text **merely names** this year's sales and next year's growth. Otherwise it looks like a blanket rejection of the same quantities the new SIGN example calls opposite. [Original design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:86) · [Revised examples](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:20)\n     7\t- **Base-effect example.** The arithmetic is correct with the next-year level held fixed. It fits the existing SIGN questions, which ask what happens when the read quantity rises. It also fits `no_clear_sign` when the supplied facts leave the effect unclear. Both new examples are generic and use no covered company, product, figure or test-article detail. [SIGN criteria and instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:32) · [Version 2 text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:305)\n     8\t\n     9\t### 2. July direction\n    10\t\n    11\tI read the seq-148 request in the dry archive, call **8744**. The total-revenue candidate has Bloomberg's **$393B FY2027** estimate. Data Center has **$75.25B for Q1**, 92% of company sales that quarter, and an AI-RAN announcement. The total has a direct full-year anchor and the segment has a partial-year observation. Read that way, the tie-break gives **v9 reads v14**. I would make “for its period” explicit as “for the quantity and full period the question asks about,” so a reported quarter cannot be mistaken for a full-year anchor. The reversed class applies the same test with the roles swapped, so a whole can still read a better-anchored part when either direction would help. [Request inputs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Reversed criterion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:28) · [Tie-break](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:305)\n    12\t\n    13\t### 3. Cross-period cases\n    14\t\n    15\tI read the seq-321 and seq-1238 requests in the dry archive, calls **8751** and **8763**.\n    16\t\n    17\t| Link | What the supplied text supports |\n    18\t|---|---|\n    19\t| `v17 reads v16` | The FY2027 CPU estimate and FY2028 company growth forecast supply no bridge from CPU sales to the next year's growth. Reject at READS. Flipping the sign alone leaves that gap. |\n    20\t| `v35 reads v9` | The prior-year Data Center quarter and next-year company forecast supply no segment carry-forward. Reject at READS. |\n    21\t| `v35 reads v14` | The candidate gives consecutive years' company totals and an outlook that translates FY2028 growth into a revenue level. That supplies a bridge through the FY2027 company base. The clause should leave this link available. |\n    22\t\n    23\tThat is how the revised rule should read. The dry run establishes the request contents and replay behavior. It used fake answers, so the three fresh draws are what test whether Jev follows the rule. [Periods clause](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:307) · [Prior findings on the same pairs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md:52) · [Dry-run result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-dry.log:65)\n    24\t\n    25\t### 4. Registration, harness and budget\n    26\t\n    27\t- **Blocking — the gate misses the READS failure.** The four F entries are sound as a targeted test for the unsupported `together` sign. They allow `v17 reads v16, opposite`, and `1238:v9` remains O. I changed only the three stored `321:v16` choices to `neither` in memory. The scorer returned **PASS** while retaining `v35 reads v9, together` in draw 2. Before sending, register **any accepted link** on `321:v16` and `1238:v9` as a failure under the cross-period rule. Keep `1238:v14` open and report it explicitly. Add a $0 negative check for each forbidden link, including the opposite-sign CPU case. [F registration](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected_links.py:77) · [Data Center entry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected-links-v2.json:510) · [Gate logic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:91)\n    28\t- **Budget — enough on the observed shapes, completion uncertain.** The existing ledger has **$0.07344613** left. Repricing the three observed job shapes from stored usage, including fresh July jobs and estimated wording growth, gives **about $0.034** for all three draws. The all-SIGN dry shape at the design's stress ratio of 0.37 tokens per byte estimates **$0.0741** in settlements, with a largest single reservation of **$0.00980**. That shape can stop before draw 3 completes. The reservation check protects the approved ceiling. Record a ceiling stop as an incomplete probe with no verdict, and use the existing D700 ledger for all three sequential draws. [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json:2) · [Stress assumption](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:131) · [Reservation check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:131)\n    29\t- **Reporting fix.** The $0 replay completed all 28 jobs with zero link rows written, and the old-wording mutant stopped before transport. The scorer correctly refuses old-wording draws under `--v2`, but its output still says the July answers were reused. Make the report say that v2 asks those jobs fresh. [Dry replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-dry.log:12) · [Mutant](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-mutant.log:1) · [Scorer output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:144)\n    30\t\n    31\t### 5. Verdict\n    32\t\n    33\tClarify the full-period anchor and the cross-period example, then freeze the two missing READS checks and show each rejects its stored counterexample at $0. Correct the July report and document the incomplete-probe outcome under the existing cap. No paid calls were made in this review.\n    34\t\n    35\t**NOT READY**     1\t{\n     2\t \"ceiling\": 0.1,\n     3\t \"spent\": 0.026553870000000004,\n     4\t \"reserved\": 0.0,\n     5\t \"overrun\": false,\n     6\t \"refused\": 0,\n     7\t \"attempts\": 52,\n     8\t \"stopped\": false,\n     9\t \"stop_reason\": null,\n    10\t \"launchers\": {}\n    11\t} 10515\t## D700 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $0.10 ceiling for the census of the link decisions before the whole-window run\n 10516\t\n 10517\t- **The question** (after council R round 13 found the July link's direction close to a coin flip, `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md`\n 10518\t  §3): \"正式完整运行之前，我想先花几美分，单独测一下连题这一步本身 … 把整个期间会遇到的 105 对候选题，每对问 3 遍，看它连得稳不稳、有没有连错。这一步不付钱买任何判断，预计 2–7 美分。上限 10 美分可以吗？\"\n 10519\t  Options: 10 美分 (recommended; link questions only, three draws, stop above $0.10, the result goes to the council before the run is\n 10520\t  decided); 先别花 (no census; the run discussed with the known coin-flip risk).\n 10521\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"10 美分 (推荐)\".\n 10522\t- **Decided (Alex):** the census may spend up to $0.10 (Jev link questions only, three draws, the writer handed no link), after the\n 10523\t  council passes its harness. The whole-window run keeps its own ceiling question (D699).\n 10556\t## D703 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses to probe a sharpened link question before the paid run\n 10557\t\n 10558\t- **The question** (after D702): \"连题统计通过了事先定的关 … 问题是它在'部分读整体'和'整体读部分'之间拿不定主意，而且有一条很可能连反了 … 下一步怎么走？\"\n 10559\t  Options: 先试新问法 (recommended: with Codex at $0, write the link question clearly, keeping Data Center reads total revenue and the\n 10560\t  38 negatives, removing unsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part; then ask the same\n 10561\t  105 pairs three times, about 3 cents, from the 7 cents left of the approved 10; then decide the paid run); 直接正式运行 (the current\n 10562\t  wording, about $7 estimated, ceiling later); 停在这里 (poc-v118 stays, the linking version paused).\n 10563\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"先试新问法 (推荐)\".\n 10564\t- **Decided (Alex):** a sharpened READS/SIGN wording is designed with the council at $0 and probed on the same 105 pairs, three draws,\n 10565\t  within the remaining $0.073 of D700's ledger. Then the paid run is decided.\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/window/probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections, copy, hashlib, json, pathlib, sqlite3\nimport expected_links\nimport read_census\nimport window_test\nfrom hivemind.views import links\nhere=pathlib.Path.cwd()\nrepo=here.parents[2]\nold=here/'\\\\''expected-links.json'\\\\''\nreg=here/'\\\\''expected-links-v2.json'\\\\''\noriginal=pathlib.Path.write_text\ndef check_write(path, data, *args, **kwargs):\n    assert path in (old,reg)\n    assert data.encode()==path.read_bytes(),path\n    return len(data)\npathlib.Path.write_text=check_write\ntry:\n    import contextlib, io\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\n        expected_links.main()\nfinally:\n    pathlib.Path.write_text=original\nexpected=json.loads(reg.read_text())\nbase=json.loads(old.read_text())\nassert set(expected)==set(base) and len(expected)==105\nassert {k for k in base if base[k]\"'!=expected[k]}=={'\"'\\\\''321:v8'\\\\'','\\\\''321:v9'\\\\'','\\\\''321:v14'\\\\'','\\\\''321:v16'\\\\'','\\\\''1238:v9'\\\\''}\nprint('\\\\''registrations regenerated byte-for-byte, v2 classes:'\\\\'',dict(collections.Counter(e['\\\\''class'\\\\''] for e in expected.values())))\ncensus=repo/'\\\\''poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21'\\\\''\ndraws=read_census.counted_draws([census/f'\\\\''census-{i}'\\\\'' for i in range(1,4)])\ndef neither(t,key):\n    t[key]={'\\\\''reads'\\\\'':'\\\\''neither'\\\\'','\\\\''p'\\\\'':{'\\\\''neither'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\'':0,'\\\\''thesis_reads_candidate'\\\\'':0},'\\\\''sign'\\\\'':None,'\\\\''sp'\\\\'':None}\ndef linked(t,key,s,read='\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\''):\n    t[key]={'\\\\''reads'\\\\'':read,'\\\\''p'\\\\'':{'\\\\''neither'\\\\'':0,'\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\'':float(read=='\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\''),'\\\\''thesis_reads_candidate'\\\\'':float(read=='\\\\''thesis_reads_candidate'\\\\'')},'\\\\''sign'\\\\'':s,'\\\\''sp'\\\\'':{'\\\\''together'\\\\'':float(s=='\\\\''together'\\\\''),'\\\\''opposite'\\\\'':float(s=='\\\\''opposite'\\\\''),'\\\\''no_clear_sign'\\\\'':0}}\ndef scenario(name,draws,should,wrong_keys):\n    rows,s=read_census.score(draws,expected)\n    print(name,s['\\\\''gate'\\\\''],s['\\\\''wrong'\\\\''])\n    assert s['\\\\''gate'\\\\'']==should and {k for _,k,_,_ in s['\\\\''wrong'\\\\'']}==wrong_keys\nscenario('\\\\''stored'\\\\'',draws,False,{'\\\\''321:v16'\\\\'','\\\\''1238:v9'\\\\''})\nfixed=copy.deepcopy(draws)\nfor _,t in fixed: neither(t,(321,'\\\\''v16'\\\\''))\nscenario('\\\\''round 18 counterexample'\\\\'',fixed,False,{'\\\\''1238:v9'\\\\''})\nfor _,t in fixed: neither(t,(1238,'\\\\''v9'\\\\''))\nscenario('\\\\''both rejected'\\\\'',fixed,True,set())\nassert any(read_census.linked(t[1238,'\\\\''v14'\\\\''],'\\\\''v35'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'')==('\\\\''v35 reads v14'\\\\'','\\\\''together'\\\\'') for _,t in fixed)\nfor key,read,sign in [((321,'\\\\''v16'\\\\''),'\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\'','\\\\''opposite'\\\\''),((1238,'\\\\''v9'\\\\''),'\\\\''thesis_reads_candidate'\\\\'','\\\\''opposite'\\\\''),((321,'\\\\''v14'\\\\''),'\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\'','\\\\''together'\\\\'')]:\n trial=copy.deepcopy(fixed)\n linked(trial[0][1],key,sign,read)\n scenario(str((key,read,sign)),trial,False,{f'\\\\''{key[0]}:{key[1]}'\\\\''})\ntry:\n    read_census.counted_draws([census/f'\\\\''census-{i}'\\\\'' for i in range(1,4)],'\\\\''v2'\\\\'')\nexcept read_census.Refused as e:\n    print('\\\\''base draws rejected in v2'\\\\'',e)\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError('\\\\''old draws accepted'\\\\'')\ndry=next(pathlib.Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/window/probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite'\\\\'')).parent\na=sqlite3.connect((dry/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nv=sqlite3.connect((dry/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\ncriteria=window_test.wording_v2()\njob_data={}\nfor seq,fields in v.execute(\\\"select seq,record_json from link_selections where status='\\\\''proposed'\\\\'' order by id\\\"):\n for call in json.loads(fields)['\\\\''calls'\\\\'']:\n    raw,sha=a.execute('\\\\''select request_json, request_sha256 from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n    r=json.loads(raw)\n    assert call['\\\\''status'\\\\'']=='\\\\''answered'\\\\'' and sha==call['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''] and not call['\\\\''archived_before'\\\\'']\n    assert all(c['\\\\''criteria'\\\\'']==criteria[call['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''sign'\\\\''] for c in r['\\\\''questions'\\\\''].values()),(seq,call['\\\\''stage'\\\\''])\n    job_data[seq,call['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']]=r\nassert len(job_data)==28\nassert {stage for seq,stage in job_data if seq==148}=={'\\\\''reads'\\\\'','\\\\''sign'\\\\''}\nprint('\\\\''dry archive: 28 fresh jobs, exact full revised criterion maps, 2 fresh jobs at seq 148'\\\\'')\ndef size(x): return len(json.dumps(x,sort_keys=True,ensure_ascii=False).encode())\ndef reserve(x): return max(64000,2*size(x)+4096)*3*0.042/1e6\nprice_scale=3*0.042/1e6\nprint('\\\\''dry max reservation'\\\\'',max(map(reserve,job_data.values())),'\\\\''stress at 0.37'\\\\'',sum(map(size,job_data.values()))*0.37*3*price_scale)\nest=[]\nfor i in range(1,4):\n folder=census/f'\\\\''census-{i}'\\\\''\n ar=sqlite3.connect((folder/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n vv=sqlite3.connect((folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n bill=0\n for seq,fields in vv.execute(\\\"select seq,record_json from link_selections where status='\\\\''proposed'\\\\'' order by id\\\"):\n    for call in json.loads(fields)['\\\\''calls'\\\\'']:\n        raw,t=ar.execute('\\\\''select request_json, input_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n        r=json.loads(raw)\n        revised={**r, '\\\\''questions'\\\\'':{k:{**q, '\\\\''criteria'\\\\'':criteria[call['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''sign'\\\\'']} for k,q in r['\\\\''questions'\\\\''].items()}}\n        bill+=(t+0.37*(size(revised)-size(r)))*price_scale\n est.append(bill)\nprint('\\\\''estimated by prior shape, incl July'\\\\'',est,'\\\\''total'\\\\'',sum(est))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
