{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"**READY FOR THE V2 PROBE.** The round-18 blockers are fixed. The case that previously slipped through now fails even when the CPU link is removed and only the unsupported Data Center link remains. [Scorer checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/scorer-checks.log:12)\n\n- **Wording and sources.** The tie-break now asks for evidence covering the quantity and full period of the question. That distinguishes the $393B FY2027 company estimate from the segment’s $75.25B first quarter and supports `v9 reads v14`. The rule still works in either direction. The retailer example now rejects a link when the text only names both quantities, leaving room for a stated cross-period relationship. The audit correctly identifies both rules as proposals authorized for this probe under D703. [Prompt text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:305) · [Source audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:28)\n- **Registration and gate.** I regenerated both manifests in memory and matched them byte for byte to the checked-in files. V2 has **R 1, W 40, O 61, F 3**. I reran the stored counterexamples. Either no-bridge link fails the gate in either direction and with either accepted sign. The `together` base-effect case still fails, and removing both unsupported links lets the control pass with the defensible `v35 reads v14` link still reported as open. [Registration](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected_links.py:77) · [Gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:83)\n- **Dry proof and reporting.** I checked the archived requests. All 28 jobs carried the exact revised criteria and missed the copied archive, including both seq-148 jobs. The replay finished equal to old-2 with 105 proposals and zero links written. The scorer refuses old-w